cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Auto-DMC-AC in your research, please cite this software and the associated publication."
title: "Auto-DMC-AC: Automatic Associative Classification Based on Direct Maximal Class Association Rules"
type: software

authors:
  - family-names: "Cruz"
    given-names: "Reyder"

repository-code: "https://github.com/ReyChess/Auto-DMC-AC"
url: "https://github.com/ReyChess/Auto-DMC-AC"

version: "5.6.0"
date-released: "2026-08-27"

license: "MIT"

keywords:
  - associative classification
  - class association rules
  - maximal frequent itemsets
  - interpretable machine learning
  - explainable classification
  - data mining
  - Auto-DMC-AC

abstract: >-
  Auto-DMC-AC is an associative classification framework based on direct
  maximal class association rules. It provides automatic model selection,
  interpretable prediction outputs, rule-level decision traces, and tools
  for preparing user-provided datasets for classification experiments.
